@startuml http_result_bean_compatibility
title ResultBeanAdapter Standalone and Company Replacement

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 8691e8800f05f28afe22499050c29220ef5b7475):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/result/ResultBeanAdapter.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/result/StandaloneResultBeanAdapter.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Observed behavior: controllers depend on ResultBeanAdapter and standalone code provides the approved JSON shape.
' Java divergence: the internal ResultBeanFactory artifact is not available in the standalone repository.
' Design reason: company code replaces one Spring bean without inventing an internal FQCN or duplicate class.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

package "Business source" {
  component "SessionController" as Controller
  component "RuntimeApiExceptionHandler" as Handler
}

interface "ResultBeanAdapter" as Contract
component "StandaloneResultBeanAdapter\nresCode, resMsg, result" as Standalone
component "Company ResultBeanAdapter Bean" as CompanyAdapter
component "Company ResultBeanFactory" as Company
component "Company Maven settings" as Settings

component "MessageSource\nen-US and zh-CN" as Messages

Controller --> Contract : normal(result)
Handler --> Contract : error(code, message)
Handler --> Messages : resolve error code and arguments
Standalone ..|> Contract
CompanyAdapter ..|> Contract
CompanyAdapter --> Company : getFactory().normal(result)
Settings --> Company : resolves artifact

note bottom of Contract
Standalone builds do not define a fake company FQCN.
Internal coordinates, repository URLs, credentials, and unverified methods
remain outside the public repository.
end note
@enduml

@startuml http_dual_authentication
title CampusClaw Upstream-Validated Request Context

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/auth/RuntimeRequestAuthenticator.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeAuthenticationInterceptor.java.
' Observed behavior: inbound JWT uses X-HW-ID and Authorization; APPKEY uses X-HW-ID and X-HW-APPKEY.
' Observed behavior: RuntimeWebMvcConfiguration currently applies authentication to every Runtime path.
' Architecture change: the target Runtime removes pre-Controller and Controller-local credential checks.
' Product constraint: all eleven operations carry the shared integration-context header examples.
' Product constraint: Runtime does not require complete pairs, reject mixed headers, parse Bearer shape,
' or expose local authentication errors. Both credential headers may coexist.
' Security boundary: upstream verifies credential authenticity and action authorization before forwarding.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "mate-service" as Caller
participant "Runtime Controller" as Controller
participant "Runtime Service" as Service

Caller -> Controller : any of eleven Runtime operations\nX-HW-ID and Authorization or X-HW-APPKEY
Controller -> Controller : bind operation inputs\nwithout credential validation
Controller -> Service : execute operation
Service --> Controller : operation result or SSE publisher
Controller --> Caller : normal HTTP, SSE, or business error response

note over Caller,Controller
Upstream verifies credential authenticity and action authorization.
Runtime does not check completeness, mutual exclusion, Bearer shape,
or whether Authorization and X-HW-APPKEY are both present.
end note

note over Controller,Service
Header names are case-insensitive under HTTP.
Their standard and company spellings remain unchanged
when path and payload fields move to lowerCamelCase.
Credential values remain opaque and are never logged,
persisted, copied into ResultBean, or used as Session ownership.
Runtime declares no local authentication error codes.
end note
@enduml
